0.107, among those whose kodak_2383 neutral filters fall in the shipped films' range; outside it: 'none'), densitometer normalisation. Then Negs's steps: sensitivity scaled so an 18.4 % grey gives raw exposure 1 per channel under the reference illuminant, and spektrafilm's grey-ramp refinement run on spektrafilm 28bf883 through kodak_2383 at data_trustability 0.3. hanatos2025 adaptation window [394.5, 19.6, 618.4, 63.9] fitted on the reflectance corpus (Otsu (https://github.com/enneract/otsu2018), Munsell (https://zenodo.org/records/3269912), human skin (https://www.nist.gov/programs-projects/reflectance-measurements-human-skin), forest colors (https://zenodo.org/records/3269920)) with a weak prior toward the median of spektrafilm's stored windows. Tools and procedure: tools/film_profiles, docs/adding-film-stocks.md.\nNegs choices: reference illuminant T, colour-science's incandescent SPD, as Kodak's tungsten Vision3 profiles (tungsten stock, exposed at 3200 K); viewing illuminant D50; target print kodak_2383; log_sensitivity_density_over_min 0.4 as printed; spectra left empty (null) outside the published wavelength range; characteristic curves converted from stops (log10 H = 0.30103 x stops); use 'cine' and antihalation 'strong' as the Vision3 and Eterna profiles.\nRecorded validation exception: the reconstructed dyes reproduce D-mid minus D-min within 0.057 D (worst at 405 nm, the chart's blue edge), over the 0.03 D criterion; the §D3 flat extension made it worse. Weighted per kodak_2383 print channel the residual is R/G/B +0.0022, -0.0092, +0.0048 D, within the 0.01 D the method accepts for this case (approved by Noah 2026-11-14).\nRecorded extraction exceptions: spectral_density x axis, gate 0.4 % of span: hand-drafted chart: its 500/600 nm gridlines sit unevenly against the 400/700 nm frame, so no straight line reproduces them (worst 0.39 % of span, ~1.2 nm). The tick labels are evenly spaced but sit up to 1.4 pt off the gridlines, so re-picking ticks does not 